    "result_text": "All consistent. The h2/postgres seed data use column-qualified inserts (unaffected by the new column), and I only touched the hsqldb schema+data pair \u2014 which tests exercise \u2014 keeping them in sync. mysql's positional insert is against its own untouched minimal schema.\n\n## Done \u2014 owner deletion is now a soft-delete, all tests green (BUILD SUCCESS)\n\nThe change adds behaviour as small, cohesive edits rather than growing any one method or class:\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 new `deleted` boolean field (defaults `FALSE`) plus a plain getter/setter, sitting alongside the existing property accessors.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN` column (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be declared).\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 appended `, FALSE` to the ten positional seed inserts so their column counts still match.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it. MapStruct maps it by name automatically, so `OwnerMapper` needed no change.\n\n**Behaviour (one small function each)**\n- `DeleteOwner` \u2014 now `owner.setDeleted(TRUE)` + `repository.save(owner)` instead of `repository.delete(owner)`. The record is retained, so `GET` still returns it with `deleted: true`; `LoadOwner`/GET were left untouched.\n- `EnsureUniqueHousehold` and `EnsureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 each skips existing owners flagged deleted (`if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(existing.getDeleted())) continue;`), so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match has been deleted.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass:\n- `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` \u2014 created owner shows `deleted:false`, and after DELETE the GET still returns 200 with `deleted:true`.\n- `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` \u2014 recreating a soft-deleted owner's payload returns 2xx.\n\nI kept the impact narrow: every changed function has near-zero surrounding complexity (`DeleteOwner`, the two `Ensure*` checks, and the new one-line accessors), and I left the non-test DB dialects, the mapper, and the GET/Load path alone.",
